Release Notes AM335x-PD15.2.2
=============================
 
- Linux Kernel 3.12.30
- barebox 2015.09.0
- Yocto 1.8 (fido)
 
Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
 - phytec-qt5demo-image
 
Build Environment:
------------------
 - Ubuntu 14.04 64Bit
 
Changes since 15.2.1:
---------------------
    * barebox:
        * Added bitflip handling for empty pages in NAND flash
        * default bootarg changed to mount root filesystem readonly per default, the init
          system will remount it based on the fstab setting. This is required for fsck to work
    * Linux kernel: Fixed bitflip handling for empty pages in NAND flash
    * meta-yogurt: minor systemd fixes
    * poky: latest security fixes
 
Known Issues:
-------------
 
 - phycore-am335x-som: 
        * Boottests showed in about 2 of 2000 boots that the SMSC LAN8710 phy could not be found.
          The PHY ID readout is wrong. The generic PHY driver will take over. Ethernet is still functional is this case.
 
 - phyboard-maia-am335x-1:
	* digital IO inputs do not work with CB Version 1403.2
 
 - phyflex-am335x-1: 
	* line in has high distortion
 
 - Ext4 write performance and powercut tolerance tradeoff:
   The root filesystem on eMMC and SD-Cards is mounted with open
     data=journal
   This increases the filesystem reliability in case of power cuts but
   hurst the write performance.  It depends on you application safety
   needs which one you prefer.
   You can change the mount option in the bootloader via the kernel
   parameters. Please note that this option does not impact the read
   performance of the filesystem.
